{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435394-v20-lore-of-clans-bloodlines-combination-disciplines-and-clan-merits","id":1435394,"title":"[V20 Lore of Clans/Bloodlines] Combination Disciplines and Clan merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-13T14:54:12-08:00","id":1435394,"title":"[V20 Lore of Clans/Bloodlines] Combination Disciplines and Clan merits","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Are the Combination Disciplines and/or the Clan merits in the Lore of Clans/Bloodlines selectable only by the the respective clans?<br /> <br /> I could see Tzimisces with many of the Nosferatu merits for example, the Tremere combination disciplines will not be out of place for some Setites or Assamites; and the Giovanni combination disciplines fit to the the Harbingers of Skulls.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the time and attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-01-2026, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T14:58:24-08:00","id":1435395,"title":"","content":"Combination Disciplines aren't, though finding teachers could be extremely difficult (esp. if it involves one of the rarer Disciplines).<br /> <br /> Merits? That's more of a ST call unless the Merit is very specifically worded about it. There's no reason they need to be exclusive just because they're in the section for one group, but lots of STs will still treat it that way; and in many cases with just cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T11:31:29-08:00","id":1435472,"title":"","content":"Of course you can use another clan's merit/combo discipline in the vast majority of cases. Some of the combo disciplines/merits in LotC are actually identical to CD/M used by other clans in 2e/ revised era books. For example I believe both the Ravnos and Toreador have a mechanically identical merit for resisting Presence/emotional manipulation. I'd laugh you out of the room if you thought the Ventrue couldn't use 'lasombra' merits like 'bigger boys came' or 'long term planning' (eyes of shadow... I wouldn't let lasombra use that, at least at the higher levels, way too strong) or Toreador merits like indelible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T21:02:27-07:00","id":1532751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435394-v20-lore-of-clans-bloodlines-combination-disciplines-and-clan-merits?p=1435395#post1435395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combination Disciplines aren't, though finding teachers could be extremely difficult (esp. if it involves one of the rarer Disciplines).<br /> <br /> Merits? That's more of a ST call unless the Merit is very specifically worded about it. There's no reason they need to be exclusive just because they're in the section for one group, but lots of STs will still treat it that way; and in many cases with just cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you allow Vitae Mutation (5pt merit on the Kyasid writeup Lore of Bloodlines) for a Ravnos, a Malkavian or a Caitiff for example? It seems fitting for certain character concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T01:00:51-07:00","id":1532761,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I wouldn't restrict any vampire from getting it if it fits their narrative. I wouldn't have it count as ignoring the normal Discipline learning rules though. A Venture that has to feed on supernatural blood that develops this wouldn't be able to buy real dots in the Disciplines they could mildly tap into without a teacher they drink from and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T07:49:16-07:00","id":1532768,"title":"","content":"As for combination disciplines, my rule of thumb is that in principle all combination and advanced disciplines are custom made and invented by the vampire who uses them. As such, nothing prevent one from hearing of a power and developing it on their own, so that some powers will be more or less widespread. And one could still develop it without hearing about it. Ex.: Brujah have Burning Wrath, but anyone could be interested in a similar power. Warrior Setites could do it comboing Skin of the Adder and Potence, with the caveat that it's less discrete than Burning Wrath (I imagine it with the skin of a horned viper, like the nickname of some Warrior Setites), but could do maybe 1 more dice of damage. Nosferatu with elder level Potence or maybe with Animalism+Potence since Animalism harnesses the Beast and aggression, but maybe they would require a higher level of Animalism (like Potence 3 + Animalism 5), etc.<br /> As long as it makes sense, I'm not bothered with teachers when it comes to these powers. VtM unfortunately does not have much of a system to give an advantage when learning from a teacher vs self-learning, which is what would be more of a sound motivation to seek out teachers and trade favours for powers. There are some small things in some editions (revised had a secondary skill for teaching, I think) but nothing substantial.<br /> <br /> As for merits, as long as it makes sense, no problem. And I like creativity, so a good story about why your Pisanob Giovanni has a mix of Giovanni, Harbinger and Nagaraja merits is welcome with me, even if it ends up with you having crazy dice pools and advantages with necromancy. If it made you think hard for a plausible story and you're going to interpret its consequences, Im going to encourage that. Sometimes the need to justify some odd combinations brings about very good and detailed pc characterisation.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 03-17-2024, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T23:21:22-07:00","id":1532800,"title":"","content":"When it comes to merits and flaws there are some that are connected to either the clan weakness or some very specific lore about the clan and would be hard to justify on another vampire, but everything should not be restricted imo.<br /> <br /> And even among the specific ones or some that can make sense on some other clans or bloodlines, some of the Nosferatu specific ones would imo also make sense on a Gargoyle or a Samedi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T16:52:43-07:00","id":1532823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435394-v20-lore-of-clans-bloodlines-combination-disciplines-and-clan-merits#post1435394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> Are the Combination Disciplines and/or the Clan merits in the Lore of Clans/Bloodlines selectable only by the the respective clans?<br /> <br /> I could see Tzimisces with many of the Nosferatu merits for example, and the Tremere combination disciplines will not be out of place for some Giovanni, Setites, or Assamites; or the Giovanni combination disciplines fit to the the Harbingers of Skulls too.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the time and attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Amalgam powers I would go with that Kindred can learn them if they have a willing teacher like my Malkavian wanting to learn Chimestry from a Ravnos if said kindred is willing and in regards to Lore of Clans/Bloodlines should be restricted to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T15:05:56-07:00","id":1533210,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't be a problem as long as the Table agrees and ST is consistent. <br /> <br /> I would warn Combo/Amalgam disciplines should be a bit weaker than the normal Disciplines to discourage powergamer abuse(unless that's the style of play). Game balance and consistency in the rules wasn't WW's forte after all. <br /> <br /> Combos learned from another or self taught would be up to ST.<br /> <br /> Merits/Flaws may be a little touchier. Some are vague if they work with Discipline activation rolls. Anything that gives a - to difficulty will be powerful. Extra dice less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}